{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-11T15:22:40.407Z","data":{"text":"The task is complete. Both verifies pass:\n\n- **Task verify** `node --import tsx --import ./tests/git-test-env.ts --test tests/docs-capability-page.test.ts`: 6/6 tests pass.\n- **Proposal verify** `pnpm verify`: exit 0 (CLI and UI typechecks, build, full test suite, lint).\n\n## What I built\n\n**`src/docs/docs-config.ts`** — `DOCS_DEFAULTS`, `resolveDocsConfig(raw)`, `docsConfig(config)`, importing `config.ts` for types only so task 3's slice stays off `config.ts` at runtime.\n\n**`src/docs/docs-types.ts`** — the capability page (with requirement/decision/code-map/recent-change entries), the ADR page, the group, and the site types task 2 needs.\n\n**`src/docs/code-map.ts`** — `buildCodeMaps` loads `getSystemGraph` once and `codeMapFromGraph` reads the `serves`/`proves` edges per scenario in spec order.\n\n**`src/docs/recent-changes.ts`** — `loadArchivedRecords` wraps `listArchivedChanges`; `recentChangesFor` filters by delta capability, newest first, limited.\n\n**`src/docs/capability-page.ts`** — `buildCapabilityPages(projectRoot, config)` per the \"Capability page model\" requirement, reusing the named spec/decision/ownership readers.\n\n**`tests/docs-support.ts`** — `docsProject()` plus `cleanupDocsProject`/`cleanupDocsProjects`, building the docs fixture (pricing `billing` + ownership, `invoices`, ADRs 001–004, eight archived changes).\n\n**`tests/docs-capability-page.test.ts`** — proves every row of the three docs scenarios.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/175-capability-pages/.run/results/1.md`, with the deviations (helper naming/split, private `firstSentence`) and the missing context (return shape and cleanup names) noted for tasks 2–5."}}
